    "introduction": "British Land owns, develops and manages commercial property in the UK, with a focus on London campuses and retail parks. It supplies space to office occupiers, retailers and other businesses, earning rental income under leases and seeking to improve asset values through development and active management. Its work includes attracting tenants, upgrading buildings and managing the surrounding environment. Portfolio performance depends on occupancy, rents, operating costs and the values buyers assign to property income. Development adds opportunities but also construction and letting requirements. Financing costs and changes in how businesses use physical space influence returns across assets with long operating lives.",
